Attacks that deal massive amounts of damage can impair or incapacitate you regardless of how many [[Hit_Points]] you have remaining. Your Damage Threshold determines how much [[Damage]] a single attack must deal to reduce your combat effectiveness or, in some cases, kill you. When a single attack made against you deals damage that equals or exceeds your Damage Threshold, but not enough to drop you to 0 [[Hit_Points]], you move -1 step along the Condition Track. If the [[Damage]] reduces you to 0 [[Hit_Points]], you are dead (see [[Death]]).

